Moonsilence wrote:
> I use "NetHack 3.4.3 for Windows - graphical interface", which doesn't 
> allow me to select the Ascii in the map. Is it perhaps only possible 
> with the DOS terminal version?

It's also possible in the tty (terminal) version for Windows (which is 
not the DOS version - it doesn't even run under DOS) and presumably
every other operating system, too. It might also be possible for some
other graphical front ends, but I guess that's of no interest to you.

It should also be noted that the tty version for Windows is save file
compatible to the Windows tiles version, so you can just save your game
in the tiles version, load it up in the tty version to copy the map,
save it and then continue playing the tiles version.


